                        "glosses": [
                            "A covering flap in animals, such as a gill cover."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e36d2ad4-4ed8-459c-8681-d51acb6d436f",
                                "sense_id": "2fd3d724-5885-3385-a6f5-ccfc5e07eb7d",
                                "text": "Hyoliths […] have a small, conical calcium carbonate shell, with a lid called an operculum."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e17fc9d9-a634-3486-b57a-f7908ff9d912",
                        "entry_id": "6762abf8-b49a-37bc-b773-53c9f37eb319",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The lidlike portion of a moss sporangium or of a fruit that detaches to allow the dispersal of spores or seeds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
